## GRADED AS IT READS (step 7's instruction), not as I hoped it would read
  - Both passes ran DRY. -Execute was never passed, in either invocation.
  - Both passes are 55 lines and identical in their verdicts: widening to -MinAgeSeconds 0 added no candidate,
    which is the point of running the second pass at all.
  - THE READ THAT MATTERS: the live runner appears in both passes as
      MARKER LIVE SCHEDULED Task Scheduler job pid 17696 started 00:09Z
    i.e. kill-maint recognises it as a live scheduled-task job rather than as orphan cruft. It is NOT in
    either pass's kill set. Searched for 'harvest|cycle_runner|17696' across both passes: 2 hits, both the
    MARKER line above (one per pass), and none of them a proposed kill.
  - This is the read HVST-bz-4 made the same way, and it is the reason every harvest pin also carries a
    worktree lock: the process census and the worktree GC are two different hands that could each remove
    what the other depends on.
